"""Acupoint locations as rules on the model (ROADMAP 4-1 step 7: 14 channels, 361 points). AI-written from the WHO
2008 standard conventions (anatomical position, proportional B-cun) before reading the comparison source.
build_acupoints.py computes each point from Z-Anatomy bone, muscle and vessel geometry and keeps it only when the
`check` patterns appear in the second source (acupuncture.com point pages) as well. Educational positions on the
model, not needling guidance.

Each point is (code, Korean name, hanja, Korean location sentence, anchor, outward direction, check patterns).
- anchor: an expression over the landmark library of build_acupoints.py (landmarks, scales in metres per cun, and
  earlier points by code). The builder casts a ray along -direction from outside through the anchor and puts the point
  on the outermost surface it meets. None = the model lacks the landmark (no skin, auricle, hair, eyeball or perineal
  surface); the direction field then names the missing landmark and the point goes to the exception list.
- direction: expression over ant/post/lat/med/up/down (normalised), or 'radial' (outward from the head centre).
- check: regular expressions the source's location sentence must all contain. '@TE11' matches the source's own
  spellings of another point's code (SJ 11, UB 40, Ren 22, ...).

Proportional cun (scale name): anterior axillary fold to cubital crease 9 (cArm); cubital or elbow-tip to wrist crease
12 (cFore); anterior midline to nipple line 4 (cChX; the nipple line is the mid-clavicular line, the model has no
skin); suprasternal notch to xiphisternal junction 9 (cChY); xiphisternal junction to umbilicus 8 (cAbU) and umbilicus
to pubic symphysis 5 (cAbL; the umbilicus itself is placed by this 8:5 proportion, the model has no umbilicus);
posterior midline to medial border of scapula 3 (cBack); between the mastoid processes 9 (cHeadX); glabella over the
vertex to the C7 spinous process 18, anterior hairline 3 cun above the glabella and posterior hairline 3 cun above C7
(headArc); greater trochanter to popliteal crease 19 (cThigh); pubic symphysis to medial femoral epicondyle 18
(cThighM); popliteal crease to lateral malleolus 16 (cLegL); medial tibial condyle to medial malleolus 13 (cLegM).
"""

